Build Qt Quick Effect Maker for QNX, cross-compiled

Qt Quick Effect Maker (qqem) is skipped on QNX and in any cross build.
Neither is needed: qqem is an ordinary Qt Quick application on Qt Quick,
Qt Quick Controls and Qt Shader Tools (which ports/qt6 builds for the
target), it compiles the shaders it edits at run time in-process
(QShaderBaker), and the nodes it installs (qml/QtQuickEffectMaker/
defaultnodes) are data files copied as they are -- nothing runs on the
build machine. Let it build for QNX, cross-compiled.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -33,8 +33,8 @@
     return()
 endif()
 
-if(INTEGRITY OR QNX OR VXWORKS OR WATCHOS)
-    message(NOTICE "Skipping the build as the condition \"NOT INTEGRITY AND NOT QNX AND NOT VXWORKS AND NOT WATCHOS\" is not met.")
+if(INTEGRITY OR VXWORKS OR WATCHOS)
+    message(NOTICE "Skipping the build as the condition \"NOT INTEGRITY AND NOT VXWORKS AND NOT WATCHOS\" is not met.")
     return()
 endif()
 
@@ -49,10 +49,6 @@
     return()
 endif()
 
-if(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)
-    message(NOTICE "Skipping the build as the condition \"NOT CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING\" is not met.")
-    return()
-endif()
 
 # Copy nodes content
 set(nodes_folders
